# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
var appHeader = new require("app-header");
var appHeader = new require("app-header")();
var appHeader = new (require)("app-header");
new require;

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.js:2:17 lint/nursery/noNewRequire ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! Unexpected use of new with require.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ var appHeader = new require("app-header");
      │                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ var appHeader = new require("app-header")();
    4 │ var appHeader = new (require)("app-header");
  
  i Here new applies to require itself, so the result is whatever the module exports, not a new object created from it.
  
  i Store the result of require in a variable first, then use new on that variable.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

